---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Engineering Artifacts - Solo Ghost"
  description="Reproducible wireless communication engineering artifacts developed by Solo Ghost."
>
  <section class="artifacts-hero">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING ARTIFACTS</p>

      <h1>Executable work, not just ideas.</h1>

      <p class="lead">
        Solo Ghost develops reproducible engineering experiments that connect
        physical intuition, mathematical models, implementation and experimental
        evidence.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="artifacts-intro">
    <div class="container two-column">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">WHY ARTIFACTS</p>
        <h2>Research should leave something that can be examined.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Engineering artifacts are part of the research process at Solo Ghost.
          They turn a technical question into an executable experiment and make
          the reasoning behind a result inspectable.
        </p>

        <p>
          Each release is deliberately scoped. The accompanying technical
          description explains the model, assumptions, experiments and
          engineering interpretation, while the executable artifact provides
          the implementation for hands-on exploration.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="released-section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">RELEASED</p>

      <h2>Current engineering artifacts.</h2>

      <div class="artifact-list">
        <article class="artifact">
          <div class="artifact-top">
            <span class="artifact-number">01</span>
            <span class="artifact-status">RELEASED · AUGUST 2026</span>
          </div>

          <div class="artifact-body">
            <div class="artifact-main">
              <h3>Discrete-Time Wireless Signal Intuition</h3>

              <p class="artifact-subtitle">
                CFO, Sampling &amp; Phase Accumulation — Python Experiments
              </p>

              <p>
                A hands-on engineering guide for understanding how physical
                continuous-time wireless signals become discrete-time samples,
                and how sampling, phase evolution and carrier frequency offset
                appear in a digital receiver.
              </p>

              <div class="topic-list">
                <span>Sampling</span>
                <span>Discrete Time</span>
                <span>CFO</span>
                <span>Phase Evolution</span>
                <span>Constellation Rotation</span>
                <span>Packet Duration</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="artifact-actions">
              <a
                class="primary-link"
                href="/documents/Discrete-Time-Wireless-Signal-Intuition.pdf"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                Read technical description ↗
              </a>

              <a
                class="secondary-link"
                href="https://mintlink.in/m/discrete-time-wireless-signal-intuition-cfo-sampling-phase-accumulation-python-experiments-a8bc58de"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                Obtain executable artifact ↗
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="artifact">
          <div class="artifact-top">
            <span class="artifact-number">02</span>
            <span class="artifact-status">RELEASED · AUGUST 2026</span>
          </div>

          <div class="artifact-body">
            <div class="artifact-main">
              <h3>Matched Filter &amp; Packet Detection</h3>

              <p class="artifact-subtitle">
                Simulation 1 — Matched Filter &amp; Packet Detection
              </p>

              <p>
                A first-principles simulation of packet detection using a known
                BPSK preamble, additive white Gaussian noise, sliding
                correlation, correlation-peak extraction and threshold-based
                detection.
              </p>

              <div class="topic-list">
                <span>Matched Filter</span>
                <span>Packet Detection</span>
                <span>BPSK Preamble</span>
                <span>AWGN</span>
                <span>False Alarms</span>
                <span>Detection Probability</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="artifact-actions">
              <a
                class="primary-link"
                href="/documents/packet_detection_guide.pdf"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                Read technical description ↗
              </a>

              <a
                class="secondary-link"
                href="https://mintlink.in/m/matched-filter-packet-detection-simulation-1-3c596ae2"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                Obtain executable artifact ↗
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="artifact-philosophy">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="section-label">ENGINEERING PHILOSOPHY</p>

      <h2>From physical intuition to executable evidence.</h2>

      <div class="process">
        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Question</h3>
          <p>Start with a concrete wireless engineering question.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Model</h3>
          <p>Translate the physical mechanism into a controlled mathematical model.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Implement</h3>
          <p>Build the model as a reproducible Python experiment.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Measure</h3>
          <p>Generate numerical and visual evidence under controlled conditions.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <h3>Interpret</h3>
          <p>Connect observed behavior back to the underlying physical and mathematical reasoning.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="public-docs">
    <div class="container two-column">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">PUBLIC TECHNICAL DOCUMENTATION</p>
        <h2>The technical descriptions are intentionally open.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The complete technical descriptions are available publicly so that
          engineers, researchers and potential collaborators can understand the
          work before deciding whether the executable artifact is useful to them.
        </p>

        <p>
          The commercial boundary is therefore the executable artifact and its
          associated delivery, not the basic technical knowledge needed to
          understand the experiment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="research-link">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="section-label">CONNECTED RESEARCH</p>

      <h2>Artifacts are one part of a larger research program.</h2>

      <p>
        These releases begin with fundamental receiver concepts and form part of
        a broader investigation into channel structure, mobility-aware processing,
        adaptive estimation and tracking, structure-aware receivers, simulation
        and AI-native communication systems.
      </p>

      <a class="text-link" href="/research/">Explore research →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .artifacts-hero {
    padding: 126px 0 112px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .section-label,
  .artifact-number,
  .artifact-status,
  .process span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 920px;
    margin: 20px 0 30px;
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 6vw, 5.4rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .lead {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .artifacts-intro,
  .released-section,
  .artifact-philosophy,
  .public-docs,
  .research-link {
    padding: 112px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .two-column {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(260px, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    gap: 80px;
  }

  h2 {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 14px 0 28px;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3vw, 2.8rem);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    font-weight: 560;
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: 700px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
  }

  .artifact-list {
    margin-top: 48px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .artifact {
    padding: 38px 0 44px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .artifact-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .artifact-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.25fr) minmax(220px, 0.75fr);
    gap: 80px;
  }

  .artifact-main h3 {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.3rem);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .artifact-subtitle {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .artifact-main > p:not(.artifact-subtitle) {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .topic-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  .topic-list span {
    padding: 7px 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .artifact-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 18px;
    padding-top: 4px;
  }

  .primary-link,
  .secondary-link,
  .text-link {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .primary-link {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .secondary-link {
    padding: 11px 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .process {
    margin-top: 48px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .process > div {
    min-height: 190px;
    padding: 28px;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .process span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 42px;
  }

  .process h3 {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .process p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .public-docs {
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .research-link {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .research-link > .narrow > p:not(.section-label) {
    max-width: 720px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .text-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .process {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .two-column,
    .artifact-body {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 36px;
    }

    .artifact-actions {
      padding-top: 0;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .artifacts-hero {
      padding: 86px 0 78px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 13vw, 4rem);
    }

    .artifacts-intro,
    .released-section,
    .artifact-philosophy,
    .public-docs,
    .research-link {
      padding: 78px 0;
    }

    .artifact-top {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 34px;
    }

    .artifact-status {
      display: block;
      margin-top: 10px;
    }

    .process {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .process > div {
      min-height: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
